[{"id":"VRCE-3-31-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":1,"english":"Then the woe began Śūrpanakhā, in high wrath spoke harshly in the midst of the courtiers, to Rāvana, given to railing loudly against all creatures.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3928acf158fd9f15676286884f2ef74d052ddb0fc03fbc45347982b5961a1141","compact":"bf949fa2a0035f72e05a8dd622ce07f48bebf09a44311a0404d34d098f01abfa","nasal":"bf949fa2a0035f72e05a8dd622ce07f48bebf09a44311a0404d34d098f01abfa"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":2,"english":"Intoxicated with enjoyments, acting as you will, and without any control whatever, you do not see that a dreadful disaster is impending.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12bc2f68adc4ce9dfe006b75cf0a451f1a5f6e53a84e5b01db7298a9d085f686","compact":"4c582c80c7d07f2a0509d19c0f03823198c1e08e4cd88039abac12130f36b6b0","nasal":"064b255bbe8911b988eba9c52fe5d358b1decf53d96dd1a1da5682758250f7d8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":3,"english":"The subjects do not esteem a monarch that is given to sensual enjoyments, in intent upon satisfying his lust and is covetous like the fire in a cemetery.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a0a3bbe7964b2951ad4ae810e9d60020e3084812ea1b5efb19294986c9e508d","compact":"b12a6730f5cab6e70f7bf52757a85270e5e2f0e281d1b59e6f24cc7697a0d5b0","nasal":"d227b63d4cce59d142d7ac05fac8c7d343b8dac398a4b12a593345600ea5e36f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":4,"english":"The king that dose not act at the proper time, finds destruction along with his kingdom and acts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b58d5a01ebc1ae4df5da67889c8d42c02e7f387dece57ed28a0b871dd8bdccd","compact":"ab0fc1fcb2570dccce5e645ade497c06678289e62b4495a25bebbfbced14e770","nasal":"ab0fc1fcb2570dccce5e645ade497c06678289e62b4495a25bebbfbced14e770"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":5,"english":"Even as elephants shun the muddy river, do people shun from a distance, the ruler that dose not send cut spies, who show now himself (to his subjects), and who had lost his independence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3b180977f50db70daa4ee14f2dfec65ed474917bf5236f930ef54f00a0ea76d","compact":"aff5838c7755c0ac158ebc7e30046afa62b3a48a424579a3fb8ac9b1a42af729","nasal":"d75fce19a53ac1768edcff3cd6b77c4c2a0358f73c19befd4ce7c4387e37c8a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":6,"english":"Like to rocks in the sea, those monarchs that do not administer their dominions, that are not dependent, do not prosper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.759,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89d385615ce931a7403201d1fc540f89da28b0ed8c64880f034f7c82dec6171c","compact":"21620428cc1dba79f61603e50909d7ee7d56827226f874f141b859c06dfab086","nasal":"c330f1256f85bc971f9c0f21ca29dd339e8436919484cd0726cc7289ba458f8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":7,"english":"Having incurred the hostility of the gods, the Dānavas and the Gandharvas of subdued souls and senses, how can you, who are fickle, and hast not employed spies, become the king?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f56858db346709dae63c9974375cc6319365db8478e8f64531b4275fef0d41e2","compact":"168ac1e668cfda6fae8c37eeabfa3a9e56231263955e360c5749a5ca777504d2","nasal":"ea9a71b48cf74e58cac21847c8b27bb1ce63250eb934388a21151f51b2d79b23"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":8,"english":"O you best of conquerors, those kings whose spies, exchequer and morality are not free, are like the common head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.762,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9b441f18b2cda9db6954d5d6c33d90aca0cd2dd4c3f5829c844a49c63e52947","compact":"413270d6e6b2d6cce663ef1bc8a8411919ad043467584bcbcb51e2d1653a457e","nasal":"0b9d66a05344a64fe52624e98035efed0ae9a7ae2e7a73af017b1c74b6758d0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":9,"english":"It is because kings know distant dangers through spies, therefore they are styled farsighted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c0782b3b0cf00df2cf26836d129e0a80e60a3a4ae61a4294c199f68592e4d80","compact":"96956775df6f447decb8ed4f35e180d03460de2d1827d8b55f0eedeac1130674","nasal":"fac500306975ba828ec02083420cecc81810e1b7dd6e906d7b0164c79a674b9f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":10,"english":"I believe you have no spies, and that your counsellors are common folks, since although Janasthāna with your kinsman is destroyed, yet you take it not to heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.625,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2980cd3481f021f86c26e97a4108ba1efa6f57a3ee2abbaac572b0b498ebd0b","compact":"7b74b3d4a2cf2464eba3a331e2b9dc40dcb76ebb884525a23eabceb647abb0a5","nasal":"7b74b3d4a2cf2464eba3a331e2b9dc40dcb76ebb884525a23eabceb647abb0a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":11,"english":"Fourteen thousands of Raksasas of dreadful deeds, with Khara and Dūşana, have all been slain by Rāma single-handed; Rāma of untiring energy has inspired the saints with courage; the Dandakas have been benefited; and Janasthāna had been harassed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6820b5f0f9c9811523f31c0dbaf67eab765013221e0fd25d203f2b3739156224","compact":"a9203d188d90efba754d19d4cd522392123ea357c360d2b36bea158e06e133ab","nasal":"a9203d188d90efba754d19d4cd522392123ea357c360d2b36bea158e06e133ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":12,"english":"Fourteen thousands of Raksasas of dreadful deeds, with Khara and Dūşana, have all been slain by Rāma single-handed; Rāma of untiring energy has inspired the saints with courage; the Dandakas have been benefited; and Janasthāna had been harassed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.918,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"131abb38d94cb70d62391b41592e6b33722baf96128af3a36146c35cb64be9cd","compact":"6cab57017e855c11cedcc017748313acc98a92a097e40b62800d7bf3b76a2590","nasal":"51dea69fd524029fc9f4e0b3fd914b8bf25085eba52dad05a260bd0a210093e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":13,"english":"But you, covetous and intoxicated and in the power of others, do not understand that a great danger is over-hanging (you).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e843d7787b5bc7ef08577da0301d1fd472de89d56360e82afc79317cae5000b","compact":"05d3974166cf10e1a71c0ae0f45a79727f0e367835c68c5ca6d08b9915631db2","nasal":"bd0fc7d5644a01c4f2aaa010b57bcdff2dfde8a4ff57a890d5f30ee54f0d8dfd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":14,"english":"People do not in times of peril assist a sovereign that is wrathful, stingy, intoxicated, haughty and deceitful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e6b2569b054ff1305e12b2bb2803fbab741dc7fef2d880b05cb9b3312041b2c4","compact":"75b7f29f9c43a52043b17e3ac8f7db84fec1fc556a57feecb6476c86451edd3e","nasal":"276cbbb2a4557f0a8191ee23d79fe558363328d53f8e76f6f690e1640c6534ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":15,"english":"Even his own kindred slay a sovereign that sets immense store by his own self, is of light worth, regards himself highly, and irascible. They do not serve him; nor do they fear when he intimidates them. Such an one is speedily dethroned; and reduced to poverty and becomes like a straw.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bc20ef3d49e62f2f192caf030120bec130f7502ba5ec77ffc589a35e7e784eea","compact":"4d2280b6c8533dcaf9afce375e08861d80fbe879d09a4492a24dacca43500943","nasal":"31a9ffdd3453841802de85e60c48bd8086bb25cff6d0ab075e2210c0689db7d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":16,"english":"Even his own kindred slay a sovereign that sets immense store by his own self, is of light worth, regards himself highly, and irascible. They do not serve him; nor do they fear when he intimidates them. Such an one is speedily dethroned; and reduced to poverty and becomes like a straw.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a957318eb5c87eb7118d0c75ebc3d7b5be9dc722388993b2dca4d51e9c651ac8","compact":"b2cb4f31eaeb16a4fd7bea81f399c5f4eafab2232fa849ef958213c7d2c50a0f","nasal":"b2cb4f31eaeb16a4fd7bea81f399c5f4eafab2232fa849ef958213c7d2c50a0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":17,"english":"Even dry wood may serve a purpose; or stone, or dust; but no purpose is capable of being served by a sovereign that has been cast off his place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f6b54184148287cd89c8aa5f34ac08a9fb7cd9937a6e5eefb795a8551893e61e","compact":"43f0d088183b4c9632995531cbe1567136d5bd4c8c8e27bf5d98188b67f775f7","nasal":"43f0d088183b4c9632995531cbe1567136d5bd4c8c8e27bf5d98188b67f775f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":18,"english":"Like a cloth that has been worn, like a garland that has been trodden, a king that had been dethroned, although able, is of no consequence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51d2657196a82a0d33c25d0707e8b7dbca5ab53fe3b31dc16b7c48e3ed878779","compact":"fcd766acc9eebea45777e3f547e369a017b8428449ce1ea9ac5d43d5a43e9a3e","nasal":"fcd766acc9eebea45777e3f547e369a017b8428449ce1ea9ac5d43d5a43e9a3e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":19,"english":"But a king that keeps his wits about him, understands everything, is of controlled senses, and grateful, and of virtuous character, endure for ever.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a203b1b5c31ff85f8723ea5216b5664b18839fabccbe697d4d27cbaa557b3722","compact":"7d4d3736ae675c42fb890db583c4186e25c235960fed6fccbb347ed76d6846e5","nasal":"c463b6cfc0408c2fc004a42f14c2c6d6b9986c2bdf66c0d30cc6f179adc290c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":20,"english":"That king is honoured by men; that sleeping with his eyes, is awake as respects his eye of duty, and (the effects of) whose anger and favour, are seen (by all).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031020","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a7c7a3b7f5de03a2a382b78e881e7e75b5e302a3e0688a4f5ffff60141732df0","compact":"cfef265bece2f3944179c82323cb7be5f375fa40535a182fa7dbf1b383a7a5c8","nasal":"cfef265bece2f3944179c82323cb7be5f375fa40535a182fa7dbf1b383a7a5c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-21","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":21,"english":"But, you Rāvana, who hast not by means of spies; acquainted yourself with the slaughter of Rākşasas, are of evil understanding and bereft of all these virtues.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031021","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8a991757fa12d2c1d17b93c11a7e3a201fa406a495ac92f72201d64a498ff90","compact":"0c78afd1a67ab70c377fd214210dfd2f51f20274b8a3957db7dc927ef447fe67","nasal":"0c78afd1a67ab70c377fd214210dfd2f51f20274b8a3957db7dc927ef447fe67"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-31-22","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":31,"verse":22,"english":"Given to disgracing others, ignorant of the proper distribution of time and place*, and never taking care to distinguish merits and defects, : you, your kingdom being in danger, will speedily meet with disaster. The commentator, is silent here. the meaning evidently is, you do not discern the where and when of things.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.811,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-33-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3031022","sanskritFile":"Ra